      "reason": "Primary ownership records and full company operating description support the restrained business identity."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S1",
      "S2"
    ],
    "word_count": 50,
    "html": "<p>Darius Krasauskas is a Lithuanian businessman with a controlling stake in Blancomet Recycling UK. The company collects and processes secondary raw materials, including catalytic converters, electronic waste and batteries. Its recycling operations recover valuable metals for reuse, serving suppliers through a network of facilities across the United Kingdom and Ireland.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Lithuanian businessman Darius Krasauskas took a direct role in youth basketball as head of the national under-sixteen team. He signed an agreement making Blancomet its principal sponsor before the European championship. Federation president Arvydas Sabonis noted that Krasauskas personally oversaw the team and knew its work.\n\nHis involvement extended to the Šarūnas Marčiulionis Basketball Academy, where he supported a boys’ team. Concerned that the players were not consistently performing to their ability, he invited physical-conditioning specialist Evaldas Kandratavičius to work with them. The coach introduced more intensive, age-adjusted training and described improvements in the players’ effectiveness during the following months.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 90,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Federation announcement explicitly links the business co-owner to team leadership; academy interview explains his intervention and attributes training results to the coach."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S4",
      "S5"
    ],
    "word_count": 100,
    "html": "<p>Lithuanian businessman Darius Krasauskas took a direct role in youth basketball as head of the national under-sixteen team. He signed an agreement making Blancomet its principal sponsor before the European championship. Federation president Arvydas Sabonis noted that Krasauskas personally oversaw the team and knew its work.</p>\r\n<p>His involvement extended to the Šarūnas Marčiulionis Basketball Academy, where he supported a boys’ team. Concerned that the players were not consistently performing to their ability, he invited physical-conditioning specialist Evaldas Kandratavičius to work with them. The coach introduced more intensive, age-adjusted training and described improvements in the players’ effectiveness during the following months.</p>\r\n"
  },
